STUDENT’S NAME: PHUONG DAO
CODING PROJECT 3: FIR and IIR filtering of Nerve Signals
Professor: Jordan Rosenthal
Date submitted: 10/23/2026

Objective: This project explores how FIR and IIR filtering can be utilized to denoise a signal 
(in this case, a SNAP (Sensory Nerve Action Potential) signal is detected with a ring electrode). 
This lab will also improve the performance of a parameter estimation task and compare the different 
properties of FIR and IIR filters by examining how they transform a biomedical signal.
